# Openbox root menu is the launcher -- right-click the desktop. Nothing
# auto-launches an application on purpose: if one wedged, an autostarted copy
# would make the container hard to recover.
#
# A bare openbox session paints the root window black, which is
# indistinguishable from "nothing is running". Give it a visible background so
# the session obviously came up, and say where the menu is.
xsetroot -solid "#1c2733" &
(command -v xmessage >/dev/null && \
  xmessage -geometry 460x120+40+40 -timeout 25 \
    "Homelab Arcade

Right-click anywhere on the desktop for the launcher menu.
First time: choose 'Install / repair Windows apps'." &) 2>/dev/null
